{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for persistent downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices during downtrends (e.g., Jan-Feb 2024) by 5-10 EUR, failing to capture the speed of the decline.",
    "Apply aggressive mean reversion after sentiment spikes: When sentiment is high (1.0) following a price spike, the model underestimates the subsequent rally (e.g., May 2024), predicting a flat/declining path while prices surge.",
    "Reduce forecast horizon lag: The model exhibits a 'flat-line' behavior that lags behind actual volatility; adjust forecasts to be more responsive to immediate historical price changes rather than smoothing.",
    "Invert sentiment-weighted bias: In periods of mixed sentiment (0.33-0.67) during a downtrend, the model fails to price in the bearish momentum, requiring a negative adjustment to the baseline forecast.",
    "Account for overshoot recovery: After a sharp drop, the model's recovery phase is too slow; increase the slope of the forecast in the 10-20 day horizon to match the observed rebound velocity."
  ]
}
